# HawkOp Shortcuts — StackHawk API, one command at a time

Cheat sheet: **user intent → `hawkop` command**, with the raw API endpoint each one wraps (in case you need to drop down). `hawkop --help` and `hawkop <cmd> --help` are the canonical flag references.

See `SKILL.md` for the workflow that decides when to use `hawkop` vs raw REST.

---

## Setup (once)

```bash
# Install (macOS / Linux)
brew tap stackhawk/hawkop && brew install hawkop

# Or download signed artifacts directly from https://download.stackhawk.com/hawkop/
# See https://docs.stackhawk.com/hawkop/#installation

hawkop init            # Interactive — prompts for API key and default org
hawkop status          # Confirm auth
```

Headless (CI/CD):

```bash
export HAWKOP_API_KEY=hawk.xxxxxxxxxxxx
export HAWKOP_ORG_ID=<org-uuid>
export HAWKOP_FORMAT=json
```

Switching orgs (without rewriting config):

```bash
hawkop --org <OTHER_ORG_ID> scan list   # One-shot override
hawkop profile add customer-a           # Named profile
hawkop -P customer-a app list           # Use a profile per-command
```

---

## §1 — Org posture summary

**User intent:** "What does my security posture look like?" / "Which apps need attention?"

The canonical raw endpoint for per-environment untriaged counts is
`GET /api/v2/org/{orgId}/envs` — `hawkop` does not yet wrap this endpoint in a
single command. Two options:

### Option A — `hawkop`-only approximation

Good when you want an at-a-glance app-level view (not per-environment):

```bash
# All apps with metadata (team, type, env count)
hawkop app list --format json

# Recent scans across the org — has per-scan severity counts
hawkop scan list --limit 500 --format json
```

Join on `applicationId` with `jq` to get a posture table. You'll have
`highAlertCount`, `mediumAlertCount`, `lowAlertCount` per scan — those are *scan*
counts, not *untriaged* counts.

### Option B — raw API for the envs endpoint (recommended for posture)

For **untriaged finding counts per environment** (the field the platform dashboard
uses), fall back to the raw endpoint. See `api-endpoints.md` §3 and
`reporting-recipes.md` Recipe 1 for the full composition.

```bash
hawk_api GET "/api/v2/org/${ORG_ID}/envs?pageSize=100"
```

Mix and match: use `hawkop app list --format json` to enrich with app names,
team ownership, etc.

